{#
  ============================================================================
  llms.txt — optional AI/agent-readiness layer. NOT an SEO or ranking signal.
  ============================================================================

  STATUS, DOCUMENTED PRECISELY (see docs/DIWEBA_PHASE_0_SPEC.md and CLAUDE.md
  for the long version; this is the short version, next to the code):

    - Google Search does NOT require llms.txt.
    - Google has stated llms.txt has NO positive or negative effect on Google
      Search visibility or rankings.
    - It is maintained anyway because other AI/agent systems may read it, and
      because it costs nothing to keep accurate once it exists.

  Never let copy describing this file (here or on any public page) claim it
  is required for SEO, required for AI Overviews or AI Mode, a ranking
  factor, or any kind of guarantee of AI or ChatGPT visibility. The site's
  actual SEO foundation is unchanged by this file: crawlable HTML, semantic
  structure, real internal links, and accurate structured data (spec §10-12).

  SOURCE OF TRUTH, NOT A SECOND ONE
  Every URL and price below is pulled from the same registries the rest of
  the site already uses -- routes.js for URLs, packages.js for pricing,
  company.js for identity. Nothing here is a hand-typed duplicate that could
  drift from the sitemap, the nav, or the pricing page. The few sentences of
  prose are excerpts of copy already approved and already rendered elsewhere
  (src/_data/home.js, DIWEBA/diweba-site.js's "oneThing" scope statement) --
  nothing here is written fresh for this file.

  Mirrors robots.txt's environment behaviour: a non-production build emits a
  minimal stub rather than the real content, so a preview deploy never
  exposes production URLs or gets treated as the canonical file by anything
  that fetches it.

  `key in collections.routeKeys` (added Phase 4 audit): routes.js can carry
  an entry before its page is built (service/smallBusiness, since Phase 3E)
  -- without this check this file listed both as real pages pointing at a
  404. See eleventy.config.js's `routeKeys` collection and sitemap.njk's
  matching fix.
#}
